================================================================================
WHAT THIS FILE ESTABLISHES
================================================================================

  What the AAP 0.5.1 per-module witness rule yields when it is measured over
  the input set AAP 0.1.1 actually requires - every JAR the full reactor
  produced - measured here archive by archive in this clone rather than cited
  from any earlier record. QA finding F4 reports that eight of the 38
  JAR-producing modules have neither admissible witness under that input set.
  This file reproduces that measurement first-hand and publishes it, and it
  publishes alongside it, as a SEPARATE measurement never merged with it, the
  same rule over the 62-archive staging tree the graph the Joern stages load
  was actually built from.

  Nothing here repairs F4. The shortfall is a property of the witness rule
  against Spark's shaded artifacts, and the required outcome for a value that
  cannot be established is to name it as such (AAP 0.9.4).

================================================================================
THE ADMISSIBLE WITNESS TEST, QUOTED FROM AAP 0.5.1
================================================================================

  > A class present in that module's primary artifact - its main unclassified,
  > non-'original-', non-'-tests' JAR - and absent from every other module's
  > artifacts.
  >
  > Where no such class exists, the module-exclusive
  > META-INF/maven/**/pom.properties file node is accepted and named as the
  > weaker witness.

  There is no third kind, and three qualifications are load-bearing in what
  follows. A class shared with a SAME-module sibling still qualifies, which is
  what makes the test satisfiable for a shaded artifact and its pre-shade
  sibling; a class shared with ANOTHER module does not. A shared package prefix
  is never evidence - every Spark module ships under org.apache.spark. And
  presence of a class another module's archive also ships is not a coverage
  verdict: it would let a shaded archive vouch for a module whose own artifact
  might be absent from the input entirely, which is the single failure mode the
  injectivity requirement exists to prevent.

  Witness kinds admitted beyond the two: 0.
  Verdicts resting on presence rather than exclusivity: 0 (A), 0 (B).
  Verdicts resting on a shared package prefix: 0 (A), 0 (B).
  Archives dropped to manufacture uniqueness: 0.

